>>>>   What he is saying is a relationship let's call it "%" between two
>>>> statements, A and B, can be represented in the following way:
>>>> A         B        A%B
>>>> True     True
>>>> True      False
>>>> False    True
>>>> False    False
>>>>
>>>>    Now, how do we fill in that last column?  Well, in the case of
>>>> inclusive or, it's True, True, True, False.  In the case of Exclusive Or,
>>>> it's False, True, True, False.
>>>>
>>>>   Now, since the first two columns are always in a standard order, we
